<!-- 
Tracealyzer for VxWorks Platform Extension
Percepio AB, 2014

A platform extension consists of three main parts, TargetPlatform, ObjectMap and EventMap.
The latter defines how to parse the trace data, while TargetPlatform defines what services 
and object types that exists in the traced software system.


1. Defining Services

1.1. KernelService - PlatformExtension/TargetPlatform/KernelServiceGroups/KernelServiceGroup/KernelService
Defines what parameters and return values that are presented, with references to EventMap/Event.
 
  Example: <KernelService name="ipc_send" operation="Enqueue"> <Parameter name="slot"/>  <ReturnValue/> </KernelService>
 
  Attributes
    - name:      The name of the service, e.g., ipc_send. Note that multiple events can point to the same Service name.
    
    - format:    The format string to use when displaying the parameter. For instance, format="0x{0:X8} gives hexademical formatting.     
                 See http://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/system.string.format.aspx for full reference.
                 
    - operation: The type of service. This can be:       
                    - LockMutex 
                    - ReleaseMutex
                    - Enqueue (Writes to Queue-type objects)
                    - Dequeue (Reads from Queue-type objects)
                    - IncreaseSemaphore
                    - DecreaseSemaphore 
                    - MaximizeSemaphore 
                    - MinimizeSemaphore 
                    - OtherWrite
                    - OtherRead 
                    - Initialize
                    - Deinitialize
                    - StartInstance (operations that explicity trigger a task, e.g., taskResume)
                    - Other (operations that does not match any of the above - no semantics in this case)
  
  
1.1.1. Parameter - PlatformExtension/TargetPlatform/KernelServiceGroups/KernelServiceGroup/KernelService/Parameter
Specifies what parameters to present and how to format each parameter.

  Attributes  
    - name:    The name of the parameter. Should match the name of the corresponding Event in EventMap.    
    
    - format:  The format string to use when displaying the parameter. See description in Service.  Not required.

1.1.2. ReturnValue - PlatformExtension/TargetPlatform/KernelServiceGroups/KernelServiceGroup/KernelService/ReturnValue
Specifies that the return value should be preseted and how to format it.

  Attributes
    - format:  The format string to use when displaying the return value. See description in Service. Not required.


1.2. KernelServiceGroup - PlatformExtension/TargetPlatform/KernelServiceGroups/KernelServiceGroup
Defines a Service Group, concisting of one or several Services.
 
  Attributes
    - name: The name of the service group, e.g., IPC. Typically the same name as the related Object Class, but can be anything.


2. Defining Object Classes

2.1. ObjectClasses - PlatformExtension/TargetPlatform/ObjectClasses
The list of Object Classes (see below).

2.1.1. ObjectClass - PlatformExtension/TargetPlatform/ObjectClasses/ObjectClass
Defines a system-specific Object Class, i.e., a type of Objects. This can be e.g. "MsgQ" for VxWorks.

  Attributes
    - name:     The name of the Object Class. Should match the name of the corresponding entry in ObjectMap.  
    
    - type:     The general type of this Object Class. Should be one of the following:
                    - Queue - a buffered FIFO message channel
                    - Semaphore - binary or counting semaphore used for signaling between actors.
                    - Mutex - a semaphore used to protect a shared resource.
                    - Actor - a thread/task or interrupt handler.
                    - ActorGroup - a group of actors, typically a process.
                    - Other
                    
    - option:   "None" or "NoIpcGraph" (Not required). This allows for excluding objects from the Communication Flow graph. 

2.2. ObjectMap - PlatformExtension/TargetPlatform/ObjectMap
The list of Object Class mappings, i.e., between object types in the Event Map and the Object Classes defined in the target platform.

2.2.1. Object - PlatformExtension/TargetPlatform/ObjectMap/Object
A specific object mapping, i.e., between between object class in the Event Map and the Object Classes defined in the target platform.
Typically there is a one-to-one mapping here, but multiple Object may refer to the same Object Class.

Attributes
    - class: Should match the class attribute in EventMap/Event (see below).          
    
    - format: The format string to use when displaying references to objects of this class. See description in Service.


3. Mapping Events to Services

EventMap - PlatformExtension/TargetPlatform/EventMap
This provides the mapping between file-format specifics and the overall Target Platform description, i.e., how to parse the raw trace data.

EventMap - PlatformExtension/TargetPlatform/EventMap/Event
Defines a specific event, e.g., a certain event code/ID, and its parameters.

  Attributes    
    - name:     The event name. In Tracealyzer for VxWorks, you may use User Event names here, as displayed in Tracealyzer (e.g., User1234).        
    
    - service:  The path of the service, on the format "group/service", e.g., "IPC/ipc_send". Group is the Service Group of the specified Service.    
    
    - type:     Entry or Exit. Entry means that the event indicates the beginnning of the service, while Exit means that the event indicates a return from a service. 
                This an required for potentially blocking services which have both an entry and exit event.
    
    - status:   The status of the service call that produces this event. Can be:
                - Success:  The operation has completed sucessfully (with or without blocking)
                - Detect:   The operation has begun but not finished (blocking or in progress)
                - Timeout:  The operation returned an error code that indicated timeout
                - Error:    The operation returned an error code that indicated an error (other than timeout).

3.1.1. Parameter - PlatformExtension/TargetPlatform/EventMap/Event/Parameter
Specifies a parameter of an Event. For potentially blocking services (Entry event + Exit event), the parameters should be stored in the Entry event, but it is recommended to 
include all parameters also in the Exit event (at least references to Objects).

  Attributes
    - name:     The name of the parameter, used in KernelService/Parameter.
    
    - var:      This identifies the tracepoint parameter (variable) for LTTng (Linux). For other platforms, this should be equal to name. Is referenced by Condition/cvar.
    
    - class:    Specifies that the parameter is a Object reference by specifying the Object class (e.g., "IPC").         
    
    - offset:   The byte-offset of the data in the Event. If omitted, offset is assumed 0 byte.
    
    - size:     The number of bytes used by the data. If omitted, size is assumed 1 byte.
    
    - unsigned: Set to "true" if the data is an unsigned integer, or "false" if signed integer. If omitted, signed integer is assumed.
    
    - float:    Set to "true" if the data is a floating point value, or "false" if integer. If omitted, integer is assumed.
    

3.1.2. ReturnValue - PlatformExtension/TargetPlatform/EventMap/Event/ReturnValue
Specifies that the Event contains a return value. Only applicable for events of type "Exit".

    - offset:   The byte-offset of the data in the Event. If omitted, offset is assumed 0 byte.
    - size:     The number of bytes used by the data. If omitted, size is assumed 1 byte.
    - unsigned: Set to "true" if the data is an unsigned integer, or "false" if signed integer. If omitted, signed integer is assumed.
    - float:    Set to "true" if the data is a floating point value, or "false" if integer. If omitted, integer is assumed.
        
3.1.3. Condition - PlatformExtension/TargetPlatform/EventMap/Event/Condition
Allows for defining conditional attributes based on event data, e.g., to define the status attribute based on the return value.

Example: <Condition cvar="@ReturnValue" cval="0" cop="lt;" target="status" value="Timeout"/>

Attributes
    - cvar:   The data to evaluate, a paremeter or return value. Refers to the "var" attribute. To reference a ReturnValue, use cvar="@ReturnValue".
    - cval:   The value to compare with.
    - cop:    The comparison operator. Can be:
                - lt: less than (cvar < cval)
                - le: less or equal (cvar <= cval)
                - gt: greater than (cvar > cval)
                - ge: greater or equal (cvar >= cval)
                - eq: equal to (cvar == cval)
                - ne: not equal (cvar != cval)                
                
    - target: The targeted attribute of the specified parameter/return value (e.g., "status").
    - value:  The value to apply to the target attribute if the conditions is true (e.g., "Timeout")

Note: Attributes are case-sensitive! -->


<PlatformExtension>
  <TargetPlatform>
    <KernelServiceGroups>
      <KernelServiceGroup name="IPC">

        <KernelService name="ipc_send" operation="Enqueue">
          <Parameter name="slot" format="{0}" class="IPC" />
          <Parameter name="cmd" format="{0}" />
          <ReturnValue format="{0}" />
        </KernelService>

        <KernelService name="ipc_sendwait" operation="Enqueue">
          <Parameter name="did" format="{0}" class="IPC" />
          <Parameter name="sid" format="{0}" class="IPC" />
          <Parameter name="cmd" format="{0}" />
        </KernelService>

        <KernelService name="ipc_sendwait completed" operation="Dequeue">
          <Parameter name="sid" format="{0}" class="IPC" />
          <Parameter name="did" format="{0}" class="IPC" />
          <ReturnValue format="{0}" />
        </KernelService>

        <KernelService name="ipc_broadcast" operation="OtherWrite">
          <Parameter name="slot" format="{0}" class="IPC" />
          <Parameter name="cmd" format="{0}" />
          <ReturnValue format="{0}" />
        </KernelService>

        <KernelService name="ipc_distribute" operation="OtherWrite">
          <Parameter name="slot" format="{0}" class="IPC" />
          <Parameter name="cmd" format="{0}" />
          <ReturnValue format="{0}" />
        </KernelService>

        <KernelService name="ipc_package" operation="Enqueue">
          <Parameter name="slot" format="{0}" class="IPC" />
          <Parameter name="cmd" format="{0}" />
          <ReturnValue format="{0}" />
        </KernelService>

        <KernelService name="ipc_receive" operation="Dequeue">
          <Parameter name="slot" format="{0}" class="IPC" />
          <ReturnValue format="{0}" />
        </KernelService>

        <KernelService name="ipc_answer" operation="Enqueue">
          <Parameter name="slot" format="{0}" class="IPC" />
          <Parameter name="cmd" format="{0}" />
          <ReturnValue format="{0}" />
        </KernelService>

        <KernelService name="ipc_subscribe" operation="Enqueue">
          <Parameter name="slot" format="{0}" class="IPC" />
          <Parameter name="cmd" format="{0}" />
          <ReturnValue format="{0}" />
        </KernelService>

        <KernelService name="ipc_subcancel" operation="Enqueue">
          <Parameter name="slot" format="{0}" class="IPC" />
          <Parameter name="cmd" format="{0}" />
          <ReturnValue format="{0}" />
        </KernelService>

      </KernelServiceGroup>
    </KernelServiceGroups>

    <ObjectClasses>
      <ObjectClass name="IPC" type="Queue" />
    </ObjectClasses>
  </TargetPlatform>

  <ObjectMap>
    <Object class="IPC" format="Slot {0}" />
  </ObjectMap>

  <!--
